From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: preserve transport buffer and frame ownership

Keep a USB aggregation container separate from the original MPDUs. Only
original frames may receive mac80211 TX status; retire the transport
container on every submission, completion and cancellation path. Remove the
transport descriptor before returning rejected/aborted original frames to
mac80211. Include inter-frame padding in aggregation admission and reject unmapped endpoints
before changing the caller-owned skb. Retire failed TXQ frames and undo a
failed PCI mapping's descriptor push before returning ownership.

Retain bounded USB worker batches but requeue remaining work after exhausting
the existing batch limit. Serialize TX requeue with the established key/stop
admission gate; explicit key drains continue to drive their own batches. Poison
RX producers and retire deferred RX work before terminal unregistration.

Pass each transport's valid RX extent to the shared descriptor parser before
it reads PHY/header data. Reject truncated payloads and headers, while
accepting a valid full-size USB transfer. Ordinary USB completion does not
supply data ACK/retry totals, so retain requested firmware reports but mark
incomplete data statistics using the existing mac80211 contract.

This does not establish an RX key-generation fence or attribute a measured
wireless delay to these source defects.

Retire USB endpoints, RX/TX producers and pending recovery before mac80211
unregistration. Terminal key/flush callbacks must not restart a disconnected
transport. Preserve usbcore authorization across disconnect. Withhold PTK0
replacement capability until RX has a key-generation contract; neither USB
completion nor a firmware TX report supplies that contract.

Not submitted upstream.

Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
